<title>FRANCE: Force Ouvriere expects social conflicts in autumn.</title>
<headline>Force Ouvriere expects social conflicts in autumn.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>French union leader Marc Blondel said on Thursday he expected social conflicts in the autumn because there was much discontent in the country.</p>
<p>But the Force Ouvriere leader warned he feared such a social movement could be out of the hands of the unions. &quot;It's my problem as a unionist that this risks to happen outside the control of the unions. More a sort of 'Poujadism',&quot; Blondel told RTL radio, refering to a popular political uprising led by grocer Jean-Pierre Poujade in the 1950s.</p>
</text>
